=== Measured wall time ===
Two consecutive successful runs, both reaching the "scored" outcome:

  run 1: warmUpWallTimeMs = 9755   (report.warmUpWallTimeMs, first run to reach the real KB load)
  run 2: warmUpWallTimeMs = 9147   (report.warmUpWallTimeMs, second run, immediately after run 1)

SCORING_TIMEOUT_MS = 600000 (src/foundry/collaborative-scoring-bridge.ts,
unchanged by this plan). Ratio of ceiling to measured wall time:
  600000 / 9755 = 61.5x headroom (run 1)
  600000 / 9147 = 65.6x headroom (run 2)

=== What this measurement does and does not establish ===
This is two consecutive warm-cache runs on one machine, not a distribution,
and not a cold-start measurement: before either run, this session had
already run `sha256sum` directly against the same processed SKB files
(tools/stark-eval/data/prime/processed/*.pkl, *.pt) and the same Hugging
Face hub snapshot CSVs to verify the fingerprint manifest's committed
hashes, which would have populated the OS page cache for those files ahead
of time. A genuinely cold machine (fresh boot, empty page cache, or the
254MB KB artifact not yet touched by anything in the current session) could
plausibly take longer, particularly for the SKB load's first disk read. The
61-66x headroom this session measured is therefore a lower bound on how much
slack the 600000ms ceiling has in a warm-cache scenario, not a worst-case
figure — Phase 23's detached-run planning should treat this as a real,
warm-cache number to plan a further, deliberately cold measurement from, not
as a final word on cold-start cost. No number here was inferred from file
modification timestamps or any other proxy; both figures above are
`report.warmUpWallTimeMs`, returned directly by runScoringPreflight's own
Date.now() delta around the real score_one.py subprocess call.
